l Slayverse cosmology note called “The Erased and the Soul-Line” . \na temporal diaspora That puts Forrest Gump to shame \nExactly. A temporal diaspora is the perfect phrase. \nIt captures all of it at once: \nnot a neat lineage, \nnot simple reincarnation, \nnot ordinary time travel, \nbut a scattered peoplehood of the erased — dispersed across centuries, carrying damaged fragments of origin, \nadapting under pressure, and building continuity wherever they land. \nAnd yes, it absolutely puts Forrest Gump to shame. \nBecause Forrest Gump drifts through history by coincidence. \nThe Hooplehopper soul-line gets blasted through history by catastrophe . \nThat’s a much fiercer image. Not cameo-tourism through major events, but forced migration across eras, \nwhere each displaced figure has to: \nread the local power structure fast \nhide what they really are \ntranslate impossible knowledge into period-appropriate forms \nimprovise resistance with whatever tools the century allows \nSo “temporal diaspora” gives the mythos moral and emotional weight. Diaspora implies rupture, scattering, \nsurvival, coded continuity, hidden kinship, and reinvention. That is far richer than “bloodline.” \nA line like this might crystallize it: \nThe Von Hooplehopper soul-line is not a dynasty but a temporal diaspora: a scattered continuity of erased \nbeings, thrown across history and compelled to make culture, ritual, glamour, and resistance out of \ndisplacement itself. \nOr more punchily: \nThey are not ancestors and descendants. They are refugees from a broken chronology. \nThat one really sings.",
