estly think it would probably have to be the Wyoming rift. \nI think that’s probably right. \nThe Wyoming Rift is the best TV entry point because it gives you the one thing a sprawling mythos absolutely \nneeds at the start: a concrete place where weirdness is already happening . \nYou need an aperture. Wyoming gives you one. \nWhy it works so well: \nThe Rift is geographically specific . Viewers can latch onto a ranch, a hole, a shard, a guardian, a landscape. \nThat’s much easier than opening on the full soul-line cosmology. \nIt’s also mythically expandable . You can begin with frontier strangeness, local legend, missing time, inherited \ndread, and one damaged man with a duty — then widen outward into Vorst, the Institute, the fissures, the soul- \nline, the mirrors, the Thread, all of it. \nAnd television especially likes this structure: \none contained mystery that turns out to imply an entire hidden order. \nThe Wyoming Rift gives you: \na strong pilot image \na recurring location \na rules-engine \na guardian figure in Jake",
